# Default owner for everything.
#
# The commit history has no single unambiguous handle — it carries several
# contributor identities (@CuriosityOS, @SSHdotCodes, and others) under a
# shared author address — so ownership is assigned to the org team rather than
# to a person. Create the @BetterWright/maintainers team (or replace it here
# with the correct handle) before enabling "Require review from Code Owners",
# otherwise GitHub silently requests no review at all.
*                           @BetterWright/maintainers

# Security-boundary and release-critical paths. Listed separately so they stay
# owned even if the catch-all above is ever narrowed.
/src/guard-proxy.ts         @BetterWright/maintainers
/src/policy.ts              @BetterWright/maintainers
/src/vault.ts               @BetterWright/maintainers
/src/worker.ts              @BetterWright/maintainers
/types/                     @BetterWright/maintainers
/scripts/                   @BetterWright/maintainers
/.github/                   @BetterWright/maintainers
/SECURITY.md                @BetterWright/maintainers
/package.json               @BetterWright/maintainers
